# Python-generated files
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
/build/
/dist/
/dist-release/
/wheels/
*.egg-info

# Virtual environments
/.venv

# Working material (local references, iteration screenshots)
/real/
screenshot_*.png

# Transfer-display visual iteration outputs — render PNGs + side-by-side
# compare composites. Throwaway artifacts; preview_transfers.py regenerates
# them on demand. IRL reference photos under _references/lcd/ are committed
# (those drive iteration); generated outputs under _visual_iter/ are not.
/_visual_iter/

# Audio cutting workspace — source mp3s + timestamps + per-route splitter scripts.
# Local-only "in-progress" archive: keep around in case a cut/timing issue surfaces
# later, but not committed (sources are big, recipe is reproducible from the script).
/audio_src/

# Audio workflow mid-products that may end up at project root or alongside operational
# audio dirs: trim/splice backup snapshots, by-ear verifier results JSON. The skills
# direct these into audio_src/ but defensive globs catch anything that escapes.
*.bak
*.bak/
_sta_verify_*.json

# Local experiment / PoC folders — scratch tools, transcripts, model outputs, etc.
# Promote out of here when an experiment graduates into the standard workflow.
/_experiments/

# Font-evaluation downloads — full per-locale Ark Pixel sets + PixelMplus etc.,
# pulled by the font-hunt harnesses (_dev_scripts/_*_eval.py) to compare faces.
# ~54 MB of re-downloadable OFL/PD binaries; local-only. The SHIPPED chrome fonts
# live in fonts/ (committed); conventions.md § "TIMS chrome text" records the
# shipped faces. Shippable picks graduate to fonts/, not committed from here.
/_dev_scripts/_fonts_eval/

# OCR calibration sources — full 2560×1440 desktop screenshots used by
# _dev_scripts/extract_ocr_assets.py to regenerate ocr_templates/. Local-only,
# only present when re-extracting after the game HUD layout changes. The
# committed runtime artifacts under ocr_templates/ are what's actually loaded
# at runtime — these source PNGs are NOT a runtime dependency.
/_ocr_calibration/
/_ocr_calibration_1080p/

# Drive recorder / OCR blackbox logs — JSONL per drive session, written by
# the in-process auto-driver at runtime. Local-only; user-private telemetry.
/_recordings/

# Overlay position/scale/visibility persisted across editor launches.
# Dev-aid state (--overlay), not source-mapped values — survives commit.
/_overlay_state.json
# Per-element drag locks persisted across editor launches (K toggles). Dev-aid
# state — prevents accidental handle drags on finalized elements; not source.
/_editor_locks.json

# Drive-recorder rendered HTML reports (output of plot_drive.py).
# Self-contained per-drive artifact; user opens locally and shares as needed,
# not part of the repo.
/drive_*.html

# Build artifacts
/version_info.txt
/release_notes.md
*.spec

# Baked font atlas — pre-rendered output of the LCD faces, so a shipped build needs
# no font software. A BUILD ARTIFACT, not an asset: /build re-bakes it every run
# (an atlas keys on font SIZE, so a visual-tuning nudge invalidates an old one) and
# copies it into the staged folder directly. Committing it would put ~4 MB of
# regenerable binary in git and churn it on every size tweak. See WIP_font_atlas.md.
/font_atlas/

# ShinGoPr6N (Morisawa) — untracked 2026-08-08. The licence bought for these faces
# does not extend to redistribution, and a tracked file on a public repo is at least
# as exposed as the release zip: clonable, indexable, permanent. Everything that drew
# ShinGo now resolves from the baked atlas (font_atlas.ATLAS_FACES), so the SHIPPED
# build needs no ShinGo file at all. The files stay on the author's machines because
# BAKING still needs the real outlines — a clone without them renders LCD text only
# from a pre-baked atlas, and font_atlas/ is itself ignored above. History keeps the
# blobs by the no-rewrite decision (2026-07-27). HelveticaNeue / NeueFrutigerWorld
# remain tracked until #116 bakes them. See WIP_font_atlas.md.
/fonts/ShinGoPr6N-*.otf
# The rule above names ONE naming convention, and Morisawa's own filenames do not
# follow it — `A-OTF Shin Go Pro DB.otf` arrived 2026-08-25 matching neither this
# pattern nor any other, so it was untracked AND unignored, which is the one state
# `git add -A` publishes. The exposure is a property of the FAMILY, not of a
# filename, so match the family however it is spelled.
/fonts/*Shin*Go*.otf
/fonts/*ShinGo*.otf

# User settings (language, future per-PC preferences). Lives next to the exe in
# frozen builds / project root in dev. Local-only — separate per machine.
/settings.json

# Caveman hook turn counter (UserPromptSubmit modulo state)
.claude/.caveman_turn_count

# Serena coding-agent toolkit (local dev aid, per-machine). The MCP launch
# config + Serena's per-project cache/config dir. Personal tooling — not a
# runtime dep, not forced on clones. uvx fetches Serena from git on demand.
/.mcp.json
/.serena/
_audio_backup/

# Narrative memory — canonical store is the origin/memory journal ref
# (_harness/publish_memory.py); local files are the write queue. Untracked on
# master so code history stays pure. (Historic memory/ tracking removed via
# `git rm -r --cached memory/` in the migration commit.)
/memory/
